Standard setup. Implement the robot class:

- static std::unordered_set<std::string> used_names (shared across all robots)
- name() returns the stored name; if empty, generate one
- reset() clears the name and generates a new one

Name generation: 2 uppercase letters + 3 digits. Use mt19937 seeded from random_device. Ensure uniqueness by checking against the used set.

Note: the test "exhausting_digits_yields_different_names" resets 1000 times and requires that each new name is not included in the set of 1001 names. So we need to guarantee uniqueness across all robots and all resets.

